<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: ICC Venture Capital to invest in Radio Ireland.</title>
<headline>ICC Venture Capital to invest in Radio Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>ICC Venture Capital, a subsidiary of ICC Bank Plc, has agreed to invest 1.183 million Irish pounds for a 23.5 percent stake in Radio Ireland Ltd, the new national radio station.</p>
<p>This completes the financing of Radio Ireland and puts the company on a very sound financial footing, Radio Ireland said in a statement.</p>
<p>Other investors in the new station, which is due to being broadcasting on March 17, include Scottish Radio Holdings Plc and International Investment and Underwriting.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
